{"id":"a3042e345de149e5","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-df-canonical-divisor.md","title":"Canonical Divisor","display":"df-canonical-divisor — Canonical Divisor","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-canonical-divisor","aliases":["58-df-canonical-divisor","Canonical Divisor"],"display":"df-canonical-divisor — Canonical Divisor","depends_on":[]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-canonical-divisor"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-canonical-divisor</span><span>Canonical Divisor</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-canonical-divisor — Canonical Divisor"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<span class=\"property-null\">无</span>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak X,X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim},K\\in V\">\\(\\mathfrak X,X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim},K\\in V\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorPresentation}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorPresentation}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (presentation predicate defined here)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (canonical-divisor predicate relative to a presentation)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorData}_S(K;X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim})\">\\(\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorData}_S(K;X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim})\\)</span> 是下游 Riemann–Roch 文件已使用的六元展开接口；其定义仅将所给数据打包为原有 presentation，不改变该文件的数据式约定。</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}canonical\\text{-}divisor\\text{-}presentation}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorPresentation}_S(\\mathfrak X,X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim})\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathfrak X=\\langle X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim}\\rangle\n\\land\\delta\\in D^{\\Omega\\setminus\\{0\\}}\n\\land {\\sim}\\subseteq D^2\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall A\\in D\\;(\\langle A,A\\rangle\\in{\\sim})\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall A,B\\in D\\;(\\langle A,B\\rangle\\in{\\sim}\\to\\langle B,A\\rangle\\in{\\sim})\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall A,B,C\\in D\\;((\\langle A,B\\rangle\\in{\\sim}\\land\\langle B,C\\rangle\\in{\\sim})\\to\\langle A,C\\rangle\\in{\\sim}).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}canonical\\text{-}divisor\\text{-}presentation}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorPresentation}_S(\\mathfrak X,X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim})\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\mathfrak X=\\langle X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim}\\rangle\n\\land\\delta\\in D^{\\Omega\\setminus\\{0\\}}\n\\land {\\sim}\\subseteq D^2\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall A\\in D\\;(\\langle A,A\\rangle\\in{\\sim})\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall A,B\\in D\\;(\\langle A,B\\rangle\\in{\\sim}\\to\\langle B,A\\rangle\\in{\\sim})\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\forall A,B,C\\in D\\;((\\langle A,B\\rangle\\in{\\sim}\\land\\langle B,C\\rangle\\in{\\sim})\\to\\langle A,C\\rangle\\in{\\sim}).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}canonical\\text{-}divisor}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S(K,\\mathfrak X)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim}\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorPresentation}_S(\\mathfrak X,X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim})\n\\land K\\in D\n\\land\\exists\\eta\\in\\Omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(\\langle K,\\delta(\\eta)\\rangle\\in{\\sim})\n\\Bigr).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}canonical\\text{-}divisor}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S(K,\\mathfrak X)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim}\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorPresentation}_S(\\mathfrak X,X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim})\n\\land K\\in D\n\\land\\exists\\eta\\in\\Omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(\\langle K,\\delta(\\eta)\\rangle\\in{\\sim})\n\\Bigr).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorData}_S(K;X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim})\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S(K,\\langle X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim}\\rangle).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorData}_S(K;X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim})\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S(K,\\langle X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim}\\rangle).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The variety, Weil-divisor carrier, top-form carrier, divisor map, and linear-equivalence relation are packaged in one presentation code.  Hence the predicate does not depend on free data hidden behind the name of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\">\\(X\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Linear equivalence is required to be an equivalence relation on the supplied divisor carrier; a bare subset of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D^2\">\\(D^2\\)</span> is insufficient.</li>\n<li>The number-field divisor atom is not used here: its carrier consists of finite sums of prime ideals and is not the Weil-divisor class of a variety.</li>\n<li>For curves: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K_C = (2g-2)[pt]\">\\(K_C = (2g-2)[pt]\\)</span>; genus formula via adjunction</li>\n<li>For surfaces: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\chi(\\mathcal{O}_X) + \\frac{1}{12}(K_X^2 + c_2(X))\">\\(\\chi(\\mathcal{O}_X) + \\frac{1}{12}(K_X^2 + c_2(X))\\)</span>; Noether formula</li>\n<li>Minimal model: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K_X\">\\(K_X\\)</span> numerically trivial on rational curves in exceptional locus</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Kollár and Mori, Birational Geometry of Algebraic Varieties</li>\n<li>Lazarsfeld, Positivity in Algebraic Geometry</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathfrak X,X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim},K\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorPresentation}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorData}_S(K;X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim})","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}canonical\\text{-}divisor\\text{-}presentation}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorPresentation}_S(\\mathfrak X,X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim})\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&\n\\mathfrak X=\\langle X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim}\\rangle\n\\land\\delta\\in D^{\\Omega\\setminus\\{0\\}}\n\\land {\\sim}\\subseteq D^2\\\\\n&\\land\\forall A\\in D\\;(\\langle A,A\\rangle\\in{\\sim})\\\\\n&\\land\\forall A,B\\in D\\;(\\langle A,B\\rangle\\in{\\sim}\\to\\langle B,A\\rangle\\in{\\sim})\\\\\n&\\land\\forall A,B,C\\in D\\;((\\langle A,B\\rangle\\in{\\sim}\\land\\langle B,C\\rangle\\in{\\sim})\\to\\langle A,C\\rangle\\in{\\sim}).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}canonical\\text{-}divisor}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S(K,\\mathfrak X)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim}\\in V\\;\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorPresentation}_S(\\mathfrak X,X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim})\n\\land K\\in D\n\\land\\exists\\eta\\in\\Omega\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;(\\langle K,\\delta(\\eta)\\rangle\\in{\\sim})\n\\Bigr).","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisorData}_S(K;X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim})\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S(K,\\langle X,D,\\Omega,\\delta,{\\sim}\\rangle).","display":true},{"tex":"X","display":false},{"tex":"D^2","display":false},{"tex":"K_C = (2g-2)[pt]","display":false},{"tex":"\\chi(\\mathcal{O}_X) + \\frac{1}{12}(K_X^2 + c_2(X))","display":false},{"tex":"K_X","display":false}],"bytes":2756,"backlinks":[{"id":"fd304c64ff2b4cf0","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"2dd1386ba4ddb99c","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{CanonicalDivisor}_S$ (canonical-divisor predicate, see [[../batch03/58-df-canonical-divisor.md]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-228","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-df-canonical-divisor.md|58-df-canonical-divisor]]（batch03）"}],"outgoing":[]}